<title>USA: Willamette says inventories down.</title>
<headline>Willamette says inventories down.</headline>
<dateline>PORTLAND, Ore. 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Willamette Industries Inc chief executive officer Steven Rogel said inventories for its major paper product lines are also down, setting the stage for improvement in 1997.</p>
<p>Additionally, he said while prices in most product lines are sharply down from year-ago levels, he feels prices have reached a cyclical trough.</p>
<p>Rogel noted 1996 overall performance was affected by costs associated with numerous start-ups and by soft markets.</p>
<p>Willamette reported fourth quarter earnings of $27,333,000 or $0.50 per share, including a $0.05 per share gain related to an adjustment of income tax expense.</p>
